User:polish the paper NAME_1. \caption{Comparison between the traditional pretraining-finetuning paradigm and our proposed framework GUR: instead of domain-adaptive further-pretraining with only LM objective and finetuning on various downstream tasks, we post-pretrain the model with LM and CL objectives on custom domain and zero-shot for NLU, NLG, and recall tasks. The model "GUR-CL" is pre-trained in the traditional approach without CL objective. The other models are pre-trained in the second approach. Without extra resources, the model "GUR-FULL" keeps the same LM ability as the model by the traditional approach and gains the ability of text representation in our approach. The models are initialized from a pretrained LM on a general corpus at the least cost.}

Assistant:\caption{Comparison between the traditional pretraining-finetuning paradigm and our proposed framework GUR: Instead of domain-adaptive further-pretraining using only the LM objective and finetuning on various downstream tasks, we post-pretrain the model with both LM and CL objectives on a custom domain and employ zero-shot learning for NLU, NLG, and recall tasks. The model "GUR-CL" follows the traditional approach without the CL objective. The other models utilize the second approach. Without additional resources, the "GUR-FULL" model maintains the same LM capabilities as the traditional approach model while acquiring the ability for text representation using our approach. All models are initialized from a pretrained LM on a general corpus, minimizing costs.}



Question:
polish the paper NAME_1. Pre-training methods which learn directly from raw text have revolutionized NLP and other areas over the last few years. Neural networks of transformer \cite{transformer} families are trained on large general corpora for self-supervised task-agnostic objectives such as autoregressive and masked language modeling. Then they are finetuned on a small amount of labeled data for various downstream tasks, respectively. This pretraining-finetuning pipeline has significantly improved the performance of many NLP and down-stream tasks such as NLU, NLG and text representation. However, these specific training datasets are expensive or not enough. The cost of GPUs and workers booms for the scaling model.
